{"id":"u-e60f45d4-4048-4aa8-b695-13c9822cb8b1","src":"community","title":"5/3/1 BBB For Bulking (Quality Accessories)","author":"Nathan M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/9dz0iD-531-bbb-quality-accessories","desc":"A four-week, four-day-per-week take on Wendler's 5/3/1 with a focus on quality hypertrophy accessory work. Intended for use during a calorie surplus and repeated four times to cover a 16-week bulk. Input your training max as your one-rep max, which is 80 to 90 % of your one-rep max weight. After each month is completed, restart but add 10 pounds to your lower body training maxes (squat and deadlift), and 5 pounds to your upper body training maxes (bench and ohp). \n\nFor accessories, aim to hit the total reps prescribed. If you fail, rest and continue the set. For example, two sets of 10 pull-ups might actually be accomplished as \"set 1\" 6 pull ups, short rest, 3, short rest, then 1. Take a longer rest and move on to set 2.\n \nBy default, less emphasis on back and triceps as these get work in the compound lifts. Emphasis on biceps, side deltoids, and abs. You can tailor this program to different muscle groups by adding or subtracting sets. Or add in the alternative exercises suggested, like the overhead tricep extension or the lat pulldown. \n\nHappy Training!","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":80,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-01T20:35:09.005Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":65},{"r":5,"pct":75},{"r":5,"pct":85}],"note":"AMRAP Last Set"},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":50,"x":5}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":2}],"note":"If you can't hit 10, rest and complete the set. Get 20 reps total. Alternative, Lat Pulldowns."},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7,"x":4}],"note":"If you can't hit 15, rest and